documentation_complete: true

title: 'net.ipv4.ip_forward Counts for the IPv4 Forwarding Settings'

description: |-
    Whether net.ipv4.ip_forward set to 0 in the sysctl configuration also
    satisfies the net.ipv4.conf.all.forwarding and
    net.ipv4.conf.default.forwarding settings. The kernel applies
    net.ipv4.ip_forward to all interfaces and to the default, and the CIS
    Benchmarks let a system that sets it skip those two recommendations.

type: boolean

operator: equals

interactive: false

options:
    default: false
    false: false
    true: true
